  "id": "cranial-electrical-stimulation",
  "term": "cranial electrical stimulation",
  "definition": "Cranial electrical stimulation is a biological procedure in which electrodes placed on the skin deliver a low-intensity pulsed electrical current through the scalp into the brain. It is used in treating conditions such as anxiety, depression, and chronic pain.",
